description:
FILED by the s526c code-generation review (Fable fork, 2026-10-24), a RUNTIME finding outside the review's subject; probe scratchpad s526c/repr/r7-decline.pl, perl 5.40.3 vs ./runpcl on main a8f0166d (code = MAIN-READY-45):

  package O; use overload '+' => sub { 42 }, '""' => sub { "obj" }, '0+' => sub { 7 };
  package main; sub mk { bless {}, 'O' }
  my $m = mk(); my $t = $m + 1; print "$t ", $m * 1, "\n";

  perl: dies at `$m * 1`: Operation "*": no method found, left argument in overloaded package O, right argument has no overloaded magic at ... line 1.
  PCL : prints `42 7` and continues.

perl's rule (perldoc overload, "Minimal Set of Overloaded Operations" + "fallback"): when `fallback` is not given (undef), an operation with no handler is AUTOGENERATED only by the fixed rules (`+=` from `+`, `++` from `+`, `-` unary from `-`, `abs` from `<` and `-`, `!` from `bool`, `.` and `x` from `""`, the six numeric comparisons from `<=>`, the six string ones from `cmp`, the conversion operators from each other, `<>`, `=`); an op with NO rule -- `*` here, also `/ % ** << >> & | ^` -- then tries `nomethod` and otherwise DIES.  Only `fallback => 1` licenses falling back to the conversion operators (`0+` here).  PCL's %with-binary-overload treats the missing-handler case as `fallback => 1` for the numeric ops.

RELATED, not the same: #972 (nomethod + bitwise dispatch, DONE), #1005 (abs/sqrt/x/! autogeneration, DONE), #1006 (the `=` copy constructor + `fallback => 0` forbidding the `.`-from-`""` autogeneration, PENDING -- this task is the `fallback => undef` face of the same table: the three fallback values give three different answers to "no handler, no rule": undef = die, 0 = die even where a rule exists, 1 = use the conversions).  DECIDED 2731 records that `int` is derived from `0+` (correct: that IS a rule); `*` is not.

FIX SHAPE (runtime, cl/pcl-runtime.lisp, the overload dispatch macros): read the class's `fallback` value (the `use overload` import stores it beside the handlers -- check lib/overload.pm / the runtime's overload table) and in the no-handler case: a RULE applies -> autogenerate (today's path); no rule and fallback undef -> `nomethod` if present, else die with perl's text (one line, trappable); fallback 1 -> the conversion operators (today's path); fallback 0 -> die even for rule-covered ops (#1006's half).  Guard rows: one per fallback value x one rule-covered op x one rule-less op (3 x 2 = 6 rows), all probed vs perl first.  Exposure: a class that defines `+` and `""` but not `*` and relies on perl dying (rare in CPAN; Math::BigInt-style classes define everything) -- low, but the silent 7 is the worst kind of answer.
